# Deployment & Documentation

## GitHub Actions (`.github/workflows/deploy.yml`)

- Trigger: `push` to `production` only
- Use official Pages actions: `upload-pages-artifact` + `deploy-pages`
- Required permissions: `contents: read`, `pages: write`, `id-token: write`
- After `npm run build`, always: `cp dist/index.html dist/404.html` and `touch dist/.nojekyll`

## README audience

Write for two groups:

1. **Non-technical reviewers** — live URL first, no install steps, CV/contact links
2. **Developers** — Node install, `npm install`, `npm run dev`, troubleshooting table

Keep commands copy-pasteable. Link to [nodejs.org](https://nodejs.org) for Node setup.

## When editing deploy config

- Node version in workflow should match README recommendation (20 LTS)
- User-site repo (`username.github.io`): `base` is `'/'`, no router basename, homepage is `https://username.github.io/`
- Project-site repo (`other-name`): `base` is `/other-name/`, basename matches, homepage includes subpath
